<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-SKF 9-mo profit seen lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-SKF 9-mo profit seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bearings manufacturer SKF is expected to post a lower profit after financial items for the first nine months of 1996, a Reuters poll of 11 analysts showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The average of the analysts' forecasts put the nine-month profit at 1.99 billion crowns compared with 2.59 billion a year ago. The forecasts varied between 1.90 billion and 2.09 billion crowns.</p>
<p>For calendar 1996, SKF was expected to post a profit after financial items of 2.73 billion crowns against 3.33 billion in 1995. The full year forecasts varied between 2.50 billion and 2.97 billion crowns.</p>
<p>SKF is due to publish its nine-month result on October 24.</p>
<p>(Million crowns)</p>
<p> PROFIT AFTER FIN ITEMS     AVG		    RANGE</p>
<p> 9 month 1996		  1,989		  1,903-2,098</p>
<p> Full year 1996		2,734		  2,500-2,970</p>
<p> Full year 1997		3,159		  2,800-3,475</p>
<p>-- Kristina Zetterlund, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1005</p>
